<InfoLayout title="History & relaunch" description="What is known about the former website, what changed in 2026 and how historic URLs are handled." canonicalPath="/about/history-and-relaunch/" lede="The domain has a history. The current publisher does not borrow the former operator’s identity, files or authorship.">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">What can be verified</h2>
  <p>Archived references and surviving external links show that this domain previously published music-technology material, including Ableton, Max for Live, controller mappings and sampled-instrument projects. Those records help explain why old links still exist. They do not transfer copyright or prove that every file attributed to the former site can legally be republished.</p>
  <p>The later backlink profile also contains large amounts of unrelated, low-quality and spam-like material. Auspicious Music does not treat backlink volume as editorial authority and will not create pages merely to capture those links.</p>

  <h2>What changed in 2026</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>August 2026:</strong> Matthias Ramahi won the expired domain at auction and paid the required renewal fees.</li>
    <li><strong>Rebuild:</strong> the site was recreated as a new Astro publication, with new authorship, source-labelled guides and rights-aware archive records.</li>
    <li><strong>Release control:</strong> previews remain noindex. Search indexing is enabled only on the verified production build after ownership, legal, redirect and crawl checks pass.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>How old URLs are handled</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A historic URL with identifiable music-related intent may receive an archive record explaining what is and is not available.</li>
    <li>A useful old topic may receive a genuinely new guide at a semantically appropriate address.</li>
    <li>Unrelated gambling, adult, hacked or doorway-style paths should return 404 or 410, not a homepage redirect.</li>
    <li>No former download is rehosted unless rights and file integrity are established.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Known archive records currently include <a href="/legacy/the-spy-guitar/">The Spy Guitar</a> and <a href="/legacy/bang-my-twister/">Bang My Twister</a>. Their pages are documentation, not a claim that the current publisher created the original work.</p>

  <div class="note"><p><strong>Former operator</strong>The former operator is not affiliated with, employed by or represented by the current Auspicious Music publication. Rights or attribution questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@matthiasramahi.de?subject=Auspicious%20Music%20rights">info@matthiasramahi.de</a>.</p></div>
</InfoLayout>
